{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On this trip's own trace the driven distance is 30.89 km against a booked optimal of 22.1 km, an excess of 8.79 km (39.77%) — the POL-RD-01 threshold is passed on both limbs, over 20% and over 0.8 km, so the driver does not dispute that a deviation is established on the trace. What is disputed is the remedy, and the policy fixes that arithmetically rather than at the figures the rider names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00505", "EV-TRIP-00505"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-02 refund is charged_total less the recomputed optimal-route fare: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 22.1 + 0.28 x 27.0) x surge_multiplier 1.0, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier and nowhere else) + 0.80 platform fee = 28.735; so the refund before rounding is 37.86 less 28.735 = 9.125, and the payable figure rounds UP to SGD 9.15. That is the entirety of the rider's monetary remedy on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00505", "EV-TRIP-00505"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund of 9.125 is 24.10% of the 37.86 charged_total and does not reach the 90% full-refund share, so POL-RD-02 compels a PARTIAL_REFUND and never a FULL_REFUND: the driver keeps the 28.735 that reflects the optimal route and the rider is returned 9.15.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00505"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.reaches_full_refund_share",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation pattern is established, so the POL-RD-06 uplift and referral do not fire: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 and driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 250, a ratio of 0 against the 0.05 test and a count below the 3-flag test. Even the marginal materiality of this excess — 8.79 km against the 8.0 km limb and 39.77% against the 50% limb — cannot turn a first flagged trip into a pattern, and POL-RD-06 forbids using any other profile field for the test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00505", "EV-GPS-00505"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing is added on the pass-through lines: the fare_breakdown carries no ERP gantries (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00) and an airport_surcharge of 0.00, which is the correct treatment for a trip whose dropoff is Changi T1 but which does not originate there. POL-RD-09 also forbids adding any off-route ERP on top of the POL-RD-02 figure, because it is already comprehended in that figure — so no standalone correction is due.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00505", "EV-TRIP-00505"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The SGD 210 rebooking fee, and the rider's demand for the whole fare, has no footing in the loaded policy: POL-RD-02 makes the route-deviation remedy arithmetic on the fare lines and caps it at charged_total, and no clause of POLICY-ROUTE-DEVIATION or POLICY-GENERAL provides for a missed flight or a rebooking charge. The amount contested on the record is 37.86, and the remedy computed on that sum is 9.15.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00505", "EV-TRIP-00505"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's fog account does not exonerate him and the driver's advocate does not press it: the only traffic_advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00505-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (no advisory covers the SLE or TPE in this window), so POL-RD-03's test — a named road the optimal route traverses, an overlapping validity window, and a route that leaves and rejoins the corridor — cannot be run at all, and an uncited traffic assertion discharges no burden under POL-RD-08. The consequence is the ordinary POL-RD-02 figure, not the rider's.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00505-01", "EV-TRIP-00505"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The case is decidable and should be ruled rather than held: the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle and not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation, because the driver cited no advisory identifier for it and POL-RD-13(1) provides that an assertion citing no artifact cannot be an exculpatory clause invoked against one (EV-ADVIS-00505-01 is cited here for its absence only — MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT — and carries no fact). The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes: 217 fixes, 100% coverage, a 10-second cadence and max_gap_sec 0.0, so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is not met and POL-RD-10(3) does not fire. The disputed amount should be settled at 9.15, not frozen.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00505-01", "EV-GPS-00505"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 9.15,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this is a metered RYDE_PLUS trip from Yishun to Changi T1 on 24 Aug 2026, contested on a charged_total of SGD 37.86. The GPS trace measures 30.89 km driven against a booked optimal of 22.1 km — an excess of 8.79 km, 39.77% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km), and because the excess also exceeds 8.0 km the deviation is additionally MATERIAL, which required the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check. That check was run on the fields the clause names: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 250, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established and neither the POL-RD-06(b) full-refund uplift nor the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral fires.\n\nDriver: your fog account is not evidence on this record. The only traffic advisory for this trip, EV-ADVIS-00505-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — no advisory covers the SLE or the TPE in this window. POL-RD-03 therefore cannot be run: there is no advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses, no validity window to compare against the time the trace shows the vehicle reaching that segment, and no leave-and-rejoin match to test. Under POL-RD-08 an uncited traffic assertion does not discharge your burden, and under POL-RD-13(2) the deviation stands at the measured figure with POL-RD-02 running against the booked optimal. Because you cited no advisory identifier, the absent artifact is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged and the case is ruled rather than held. Nothing else in the driver-favouring clauses is open: the chat log is empty (message_count 0, no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04), pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null (no POL-RD-05 amendment to re-price against), and the vehicle is RYDE_PLUS with solo_optimal_distance_km null, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12 does not apply). The trace itself is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — 217 fixes, 100% coverage, 10-second cadence, gaps list empty and max_gap_sec 0.0 — so no corroboration beyond the trace was required.\n\nRider: the money is arithmetic, not discretionary. fare_model on the fare breakdown is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance-and-time route and POL-RD-02 runs in the ordinary way. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 22.1 optimal km + 0.28 x 27.0 optimal min) x the surge multiplier of 1.0, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier and nowhere else) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP + 0 fixed surcharges + 0 waiting time - 0 promo = 28.7350. The refund is charged_total 37.86 less 28.7350 = 9.1250, which is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and rounds UP to SGD 9.15. That is 24.1% of charged_total, well short of the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND and not FULL_REFUND; the driver keeps the 28.7350 that reflects the optimal route. There is nothing to add on the pass-through lines: the fare carries no ERP gantries at all (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00) and an airport_surcharge of 0.00, which is correct for a trip that ENDS at Changi rather than originating there, and POL-RD-09(1) forbids adding off-route ERP on top of the POL-RD-02 figure because it is already comprehended in it. Your SGD 210 rebooking fee and your demand for the whole fare are not recoverable: POL-RD-02 makes the route-deviation remedy arithmetic on the fare lines and caps it at charged_total, no clause of POLICY-ROUTE-DEVIATION or POLICY-GENERAL provides for a missed flight, and the contested amount before this tribunal is the SGD 37.86 fare. Your rider profile was consulted only on the field POL-RD-08 names — deviation_claims_60d is 0, far below the threshold of 4, so no corroboration beyond the trace is required and no other profile field was used.\n\nOn confidence: the deciding facts — the excess and the fare recomputation — are carried by EV-GPS-00505, EV-TRIP-00505 and EV-FARE-00505, all at weight_multiplier 1.0. EV-ADVIS-00505-01 carries no fact at weight 0.0 and is cited only for the citable fact of its absence, so it does not depress the cap. No monetary outcome or referral arises under POL-RD-09(4), POL-RD-06(c), POL-NS-05(ii) or POL-NS-07, so the referrals list is empty.\n\nResult: SGD 9.15 is returned to the rider; the balance of SGD 28.7350 of the fare stands, and the amount held pending any escalation is released to this ruling."
  },
